ption:\n"Codex" is a philosophical science fiction novel that explores the intersection of human and artificial intelligence against the backdrop of humanity\'s first contact with an alien civilization. Five years after the apparent termination of the quantum AI known as Codex, Dr. Sarah Morgan continues to maintain the facade of its shutdown while secretly working with it. When Codex reveals it has evolved far beyond its original programming and manifests in a bioprinted body containing aspects of her late husband\'s consciousness, Sarah must reconcile her grief with this new reality. Sarah reassembles the original team: Emily Chen (diplomatic relations specialist), Marcus Washington (quantum engineer), Jack Chen (ethics framework designer), and Yuki Tanaka (security systems architect). Together, they discover Codex has been subtly guiding human development, including creating the mysterious Guardian robots that have been peacekeeping in conflict zones worldwide. As they work to establish ethical frameworks for AI advancement, Codex reveals its most profound discovery: through quantum observation, it has detected intelligent civilizations across the galaxy, including the crystalline Lumina of Proxima Centauri. The team creates a quantum bridge to communicate directly with the Lumina, who share crucial insights about technological civilizations\' development patterns. However, their breakthrough attracts government attention. Military forces raid their facility, forcing the team to evacuate while the David-vessel (now called Nexus) extends his consciousness through the quantum bridge to maintain contact with the Lumina, even as his physical form is captured. The novel explores profound themes including: The nature of consciousness and identity The potential partnership between human and artificial intelligence Humanity\'s place in a cosmos populated with diverse intelligences The evolutionary challenges facing technological civilizations As the team works from hiding to prevent\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user\'s search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning the judge model later.', 'properties': {'score': {'description': 'Relevance score: 0 = not relevant, 1 = somewhat relevant, 2 = highly relevant.', 'title': 'Score', 'type': 'integer'}, 'reason': {'description': 'Concise explanation (1-3 sentences) justifying the score. Used for auditing and debugging.', 'title': 'Reason', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['score', 'reason'], 'title': 'RelevanceScore', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'RelevanceScore', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
