ok Two of This Renowned Dragon Graphic Novel Series A Boy. A Dragon. And the Cost of Choosing Peace. Return to the world of Glacias, where long-standing fear and tradition keep dragons and humans dividedand where one boys growing resolve could change everything. Juka, an orphan bound by fate to his water dragon Lyth, continues his journey to bring understanding between two worlds taught to fear one another. Joined by the fiery and determined Aleria, Juka faces a dangerous new trial: a tense encounter with a mysterious fire dragonand a driven dragon hunter searching for purpose and proof. As their path unfolds, Juka and Aleria uncover the haunting history of two brothers torn between duty and conscience. The Hyosha Dragon Hunter Guild is more than an adversaryit is a legacy shaped by fear, loss, and rigid tradition. And Juka is determined to challenge that legacy. With Lyths fluid grace and Alerias powerful new companionthe fierce and wounded dragon Thaeronevery choice carries weight. Trust is tested. Old beliefs are questioned. And the dream of coexistence demands courage, empathy, and sacrifice. For the Kidsand AdultsWho Grew Up Around Dice and Dragons If you grew up with Dungeons & Dragons, and now youre raising a child who dreams in dragons and magic, Glacias is a story meant to be shared. Inspired by the spirit of tabletop storytelling, this comic blends fantasy adventure, emotional depth, and cinematic visualscapturing the imagination of young readers while offering meaningful themes for older fans. Whether your child is discovering fantasy for the first time or stepping into their own coming-of-age journey, Glacias grows with them. Whats Inside: - A double-length fantasy flipbook (Issues 34) - Full-color comic pages with dynamic, cinematic paneling - All-ages friendlyaccessible for kids, layered enough for adults - Digital format for Kindle, tablets, and comic reading apps Perfect For Fans Of: - Dungeons and Dragons - How to Train Your Dragon - Avatar:\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user's search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n", 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning the judge model later.', 'properties': {'score': {'description': 'Relevance score: 0 = not relevant, 1 = somewhat relevant, 2 = highly relevant.', 'title': 'Score', 'type': 'integer'}, 'reason': {'description': 'Concise explanation (1-3 sentences) justifying the score. Used for auditing and debugging.', 'title': 'Reason', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['score', 'reason'], 'title': 'RelevanceScore', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'RelevanceScore', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
